  "query_preview": "..\nAs of 108 AM Tuesday...\n\nKEY MESSAGE 1... Hot temperatures return mid through late week. A \nslow moving cold front will bring a good shot at showers and \nthunderstorms and much needed rain/cooler temperatures, especially \nover the weekend. \n\nIt appears widespread 90+ degree temperatures will return Thursday \nand Friday as surface high pressure will be offshore and the \nmid/upper level ridging will shift to the SE states. It appears the \nhottest day will likely be Thursday under the ridge. A break in the \nridge and a developing Ohio Valley to central Appalachians trough \nwill approach Friday lowering mid level heights enough so that the \ntemperatures may back off a few degrees. Expect lower to mid 90s \non Thursday and upper 80s to lower 90s Friday. These temperatures \nwill back off considerably this weekend as the upper trough develops \nover the Ohio into the TN valley region increasing moisture, \ncloudiness. and likely showers/storms over the weekend. Expect highs \nin the 80s except around 90 in the SE.\n\nThe aforementioned approaching trough will also be accompanied by a \npre-frontal trough and a surface front (or two). These features \nshould allow for a likelihood 60-70 percent chance of mainly PM \nshowers/storms both Saturday and Sunday. We will update any severe \nthreat in upcoming forecasts. At the moment, it appears wind shear \nmay be lacking but instability will be high.",
